<!-- Welcome Section -->

## Welcome
    
This professional learning module is designed to help you prepare to teach CodeAI's        **Foundations of AI Programming [JavaScript]** from the <a href="https://studio.code.org/courses/artificial-intelligence-foundations-2026" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AI Foundations Curriculum</a>.

The Programming with AI content is designed for 9th - 12th grade students.
    


<!-- Goals Section -->
<div style="margin: 20px auto; width: 90%; max-width: 900px; background: #f7f8fa; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); font-size: 14pt;">
    <h2 style="margin-top: 0;">In this module, you will:</h2>
    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; font-size: 14pt">
        <li>Recognize AI as a pattern-matching tool, not a black box, and teach students to evaluate its output rather than accept it.</li><br>
        <li>Guide students through structured planning documents (prompt.md, spec.md) as the bridge between an idea and a working prompt.</li><br>
        <li>Explain the HTML/CSS split and the DOM as separate, teachable mental models, not implementation details.</li><br>
        <li>Apply the POUR accessibility framework to audit real sites and recognize how AI reproduces existing accessibility failures.</li><br>
        <li>Support students through the core JavaScript progression as a connected sequence, not isolated topics. This includes events, variables/state, functions, conditionals, and loops.
</li>
    </ul>
</div>


**Suggested Total Time:** 90 minutes

**Lesson One Suggested Time:** 10 minutes

---

##Take the Pre-Survey

CodeAI values and is responsive to feedback. Please fill out the pre-survey to  tell us about who you are and how we can best support you.


<p style="text-align: left;">
<a class="btn btn-large btn-primary" href="https://studio.code.org/form/exploring_generative_ai_selfpaced_pl_pre_survey" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Take the pre-survey</a>
</p>


